{
  "surface": "gcp/cloud-asset-inventory-compute-instance",
  "provider": "gcp",
  "reference": {
    "title": "Export asset metadata to BigQuery (official BigQuery schemas) + Method: exportAssets (REST v1)",
    "url": "https://cloud.google.com/asset-inventory/docs/exporting-to-bigquery",
    "consulted_at": "2026-10-14"
  },
  "delivery": {
    "kind": "bigquery",
    "path_template": "projects/{projectId}/datasets/{datasetId}/{table} (per-asset-type: {table}_{assetType with non-alphanumerics replaced by _})",
    "format": "bigquery-native-table",
    "compression": "not-applicable"
  },
  "reference_urls": {
    "export_assets_rest": "https://cloud.google.com/asset-inventory/docs/reference/rest/v1/TopLevel/exportAssets",
    "asset_message": "https://cloud.google.com/asset-inventory/docs/reference/rest/v1/Asset",
    "gcs_export": "https://cloud.google.com/asset-inventory/docs/exporting-to-cloud-storage",
    "supported_asset_types": "https://cloud.google.com/asset-inventory/docs/supported-asset-types"
  },
  "notes": [
    "The export mechanism genuinely exists and is officially documented: Cloud Asset Inventory ExportAssets, destinations Cloud Storage (newline-delimited JSON, one google.cloud.asset.v1.Asset per line) and BigQuery (fields stored as columns).",
    "Three BigQuery schemas are published verbatim by Google: Resource schema, IAM policy schema, Organization policy schema. They are transcribed below.",
    "RESOURCE single-table schema stores resource.data as a STRING holding JSON. With separateTablesPerAssetType=true the schema instead maps nested Resource.data fields to RECORD columns (up to 15 nested levels) - but Google publishes NO per-asset-type schema for compute.googleapis.com/Instance.",
    "Therefore the concrete shape of resource.data for compute.googleapis.com/Instance is UNVERIFIED and listed in 'unverified'.",
    "Casing rule (documented): RESOURCE + per-asset-type tables use camelCase (e.g. assetType); all other content types use snake_case (e.g. asset_type).",
    "BigQuery types below are transcribed exactly as published (STRING, RECORD, TIMESTAMP, INTEGER, BOOLEAN, REPEATED/NULLABLE modes).",
    "Sets: Cloud Asset Inventory publishes SEVERAL distinct schemas selected by contentType (RESOURCE / IAM_POLICY / ORG_POLICY) plus the REST message envelopes. The same column name (name, asset_type, ancestors, update_time, resource, readTime) legitimately recurs across different schemas, so each schema is its own set and the name collisions are intentional."
  ],
  "sets": [
